+// ── the one-pass row: a running threshold, no histogram ────────────────────
+// docs/experiments/20261020_onepass/ has the probe and the design.  Elements
+// above the running threshold stage into the arena; when the count crosses
+// `topk + kOnePassB2` the CTA compacts -- it selects the exact top-k of
+// (survivors ∪ arena), raises the threshold to their k-th, and drops the
+// rest.  The survivors live in `output` (the contract's staging buffer)
+// between compacts, the arena is scratch, and the compact's gather goes to
+// the arena front and is then copied to `output`, so no region is read and
+// written at once.  Every element is read from DRAM exactly once, and the
+// shared atomics fire only on candidates (~k·ln(L/B) per row) -- which is
+// what moves the 28/32-AP parts off the per-element atomic issue ceiling
+// that caps the two-pass row near half the wall.
+//
+// The invariant (upstream's): an element dropped at a compact is below at
+// least k elements of the same row at that moment, so it can never be in the
+// row's top-k; the threshold only rises.  A row whose count never reaches
+// `topk` (every element key == 0) is a row of negative NaNs -- the only
+// zero-key encoding -- and is answered by the NaN disposition, never by this
+// select.
+constexpr uint32_t kOnePassB2 = 256;
+
+// The arena's entries: `topk + B2` for the compact trigger, plus one vote
+// period of staging.  One outer iteration stages up to BLOCK_SIZE * 16
+// elements (two blocks per 8-lane group), so the slack is that exactly --
+// anything smaller overflows the arena between votes (measured, as a crash).
+constexpr uint32_t onepass_slack(uint32_t topk) {
+    (void)topk;
+    return 8192;
+}
+
+template <uint32_t BLOCK_SIZE>
+constexpr uint32_t onepass_arena_entries(uint32_t topk) {
+    return topk + kOnePassB2 + onepass_slack(topk);
+}
+
+// The host-visible half of the gate (the device adds alignment and the
+// per-row window): 128 KiB-smem families, long rows, the swept k set.
+// k = 2048 is out: its arena cannot hold the key sidecar at any useful
+// occupancy.
+constexpr bool onepass_shape_applies(uint32_t vocab_size, uint32_t topk) {
+    return ARCH_SMEM_PER_AP_BYTES >= 128 * 1024 && vocab_size >= 65536 &&
+           (topk == 512 || topk == 1024);
+}
